;; agent$drive (RFC-073 "The drive loop", byj-71w.6): /drive. Works through
;; the project's goal one bead at a time — the next ready bead under the
;; profile's epic, worked in a ReAct turn of its own, checked, judged, and
;; closed as the profile says — and stops where the profile says to ask.
;;
;; Its loop is brainyard/loops/drive.edn. Each bead's turn is the bundled
;; ReAct loop with every tool the session has, so the work is done as any
;; turn's is, under the same permission gate and the profile's holds on it
;; (RFC-012); the drive$* commands are what its :config turns on.
{:description
 "Works through this project's goal under its profile (.brainyard/profile.edn, which /init writes on the person's yes): picks the next ready bead of the project's beads, works it in a turn of its own, checks the work tree and the bead, closes it as the profile allows, and goes on — asking the person only where the profile says to, and stopping at the profile's limits, on a question, or when nothing is ready. Ends with each bead's outcome. Takes minutes to hours."

 :instruction-resource "brainyard/prompts/agents/drive.md"

 :loop "brainyard/loops/drive.edn"

 ;; every tool the session has, for the bead's work; but not itself
 :deny-tools ["agent$drive"]

 ;; it asks the person as it works, so its call is waited on, never detached
 :attended? true

 :tier :standard

 :config {:drive-tools? true}}
